/T (A landslide is the downward movement of soil, rock, or debris along a slope due to gravity. It occurs when slope stability is reduced by factors such as heavy rainfall, earthquakes, volcanic activity, or human actions like deforestation and construction. Landslides may happen suddenly or develop slowly and are common in hilly and mountainous regions. They pose serious threats to human life, infrastructure, and the natural environment.)
/E (A landslide is the downward movement of soil, rock, or debris along a slope due to gravity. It occurs when slope stability is reduced by factors such as heavy rainfall, earthquakes, volcanic activity, or human actions like deforestation and construction. Landslides may happen suddenly or develop slowly and are common in hilly and mountainous regions. They pose serious threats to human life, infrastructure, and the natural environment.)
